CRASH-26: reject a status value in a rule premise that is not on a link

newpremise() accepted OPEN, CLOSED or ACTIVE as the value of any
premise, so "IF TANK T1 LEVEL IS OPEN" loaded. checkpremise() sends any
premise with a status to checkstatus(), which reads LinkStatus at the
premise's index: here a node index, past the end of the array when the
node's index is larger than the number of links. A status value is now
an illegal value (202) unless the premise is on a link.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply CRASH-26_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/rules.c b/src/rules.c
index 1b009ad..6f4f42b 100644
--- a/src/rules.c
+++ b/src/rules.c
@@ -833,6 +833,9 @@ int newpremise(Project *pr, int logop)
         if (v == r_FILLTIME || v == r_DRAINTIME) x = x * 3600.0;
     }
 
+    // Only a link has a status to compare with
+    if (s > IS_NUMBER && i != r_LINK) return 202;
+
     // Create new premise structure
     p = (Spremise *)malloc(sizeof(Spremise));
     if (p == NULL) return 101;
